# Grid results: track the analysis inputs, drop the bulk
#
# scripts/common.get_canonical_output_dir writes every run under outputs/, and
# scripts/analysis.py rebuilds every reported table from the per-run CSV/JSONL
# there. The 183-run grid executes on a shared VM we do not administer, so those
# inputs need a path off that host; WandB carries the metrics but not the Hydra
# config, the run log, or sweep_status.json.
#
# Checkpoints (final_global_model.pt, ~27 MB each) stay untracked -- they are
# several GB across the grid and nothing reported is computed from them.
#
# This block must stay at the END of the file: `*.log` above would otherwise
# re-ignore run.log, since the last matching pattern wins.
outputs/**
!outputs/**/
!outputs/**/experiment_log.csv
!outputs/**/experiment_log.jsonl
!outputs/**/run.log
!outputs/**/.hydra/*.yaml
!outputs/**/sweep_status.json

# Legacy pre-matrix Hydra runs land in outputs/<date>/<time>/ rather than the
# canonical outputs/<phase>/... taxonomy. They are local scratch, not grid
# results, so re-ignore them after the negations above.
outputs/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# Scratch phases. The reported grid runs under phase `formal` (the 183-run
# confirmatory matrices) and `explore` (pass2/pass3 staging); `ci`, `smoke` and
# `golden` are throwaway validation runs. Deliberately an exclusion list rather
# than an allowlist of the two real phases: a phase name added later should
# default to being kept, since silently dropping results is the costlier failure.
outputs/ci/
outputs/smoke/
outputs/golden/
